<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">death</ansi>

When your hitpoints fall to zero or less, you'll drop to the ground and begin
to bleed out. While bleeding out, each round you'll fall more and more into
the negative range. Any spells you were casting are lost.

Once you reach -10 hitpoints, you will die!

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Death Penalties:</ansi>
  - One of your core attributes will permanently weaken slightly.
  - Skills you haven't practiced recently may grow rusty and diminish.
  - You'll be transported home with all pools restored.

The best defense against death is staying aware of your health and knowing
when to <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>. Skills and attributes you use regularly are protected
from decay -- keep training and they'll endure.

